      "notes": [
        "This unloaded rear-hand straight punch is an authored joint-space task, not a generic strike retarget. The right fist starts in a rear/down chamber and advances mainly forward/up along a nearly constant lateral lane as the pelvis and trunk lead the shoulder/elbow extension, then retracts to a compact torso-side reset. Published boxing kinematics inform the phase order and predominantly linear path; the exact angles are engineering approximations, not an athlete-specific capture.",
        "The left arm remains in the reduced model’s cheek/upper-chest guard. Its visible skin fist uses independently authored thumb and finger joint targets; left finger muscle torques are not simulated. The hand closure is a rigging approximation for a readable clenched fist.",
        "A modest knee/hip load and pelvis-first turn precede trunk follow-through and elbow extension. Published boxing studies report lower-body support, trunk rotation and elbow contribution in the cross, with athlete-specific timing. The joint angles remain bounded engineering targets, not a validated boxing performance.",
        "Both feet remain on fixed support fixtures; this prototype cannot model a rear-foot pivot, stance step, impact or measured ground-reaction impulse. The output is a bounded muscle-driven forward-simulation replay, not a live physics engine or a calibrated boxing-performance prediction.",
        "The right wrist and fingers use action keyframe retargeting on the continuous skin. The physical MyoSim right-arm and wrist states remain in the record; the visible two-fist guard and near-neutral punch wrist are display targets. This does not model glove contact, deformable skin, bone stress, collision or injury risk."
      ],
